{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02450",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.28,
      "end_seconds": 4.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Hi doctor, am I too early?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.67,
      "end_seconds": 10.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.98,
      "end_seconds": 39.24,
      "duration_seconds": 27.26,
      "text": "So, I've been getting up at night to pass urine, doctor. I've never really been one for hospitals. Oh, uh, and dribbling after passing urine. And a feeling of not emptying as well, since yesterday. Hmm, uh, with feeling of not emptying, severe, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.6,
      "end_seconds": 45.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.23,
      "end_seconds": 54.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.64,
      "end_seconds": 77.81,
      "duration_seconds": 10.17,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 119 over 68, oxygen saturation is 98 percent. And pulse 70, temperature is 36.8 degrees. Has there been any weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.7,
      "end_seconds": 82.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "No, you know, no weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.28,
      "end_seconds": 90.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "Any burning on passing urine, back pain or blood in the urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.53,
      "end_seconds": 100.53,
      "duration_seconds": 9.0,
      "text": "Well, uh, no, no burning on passing urine, back pain or blood in the urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.9,
      "end_seconds": 103.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Understood. Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.53,
      "end_seconds": 106.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.93,
      "end_seconds": 109.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.71,
      "end_seconds": 112.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.03,
      "end_seconds": 116.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.95,
      "end_seconds": 128.83,
      "duration_seconds": 8.88,
      "text": "I had an operation for a hernia last spring. Sorry, uh, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.29,
      "end_seconds": 147.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.57,
      "end_seconds": 161.39,
      "duration_seconds": 12.82,
      "text": "Right, you know, yes, naproxen. I've no idea what the reaction was, only that I'm not supposed to have it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.91,
      "end_seconds": 177.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.83,
      "end_seconds": 189.51,
      "duration_seconds": 10.68,
      "text": "Arthritis in my knees, for five years. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. Yes, gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.9,
      "end_seconds": 199.6,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "Okay, I can see gout in your file as well. What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.62,
      "end_seconds": 215.17,
      "duration_seconds": 10.55,
      "text": "Paracetamol. I take it 650 milligrams, when needed. Febuxostat. I take it 80 milligrams, once a day for the gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.95,
      "end_seconds": 219.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.19,
      "end_seconds": 225.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.64,
      "end_seconds": 229.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.44,
      "end_seconds": 236.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.19,
      "end_seconds": 241.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Listening to the whole story, this is probably benign prostate enlargement."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.63,
      "end_seconds": 250.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.39,
      "end_seconds": 260.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.86,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now benign prostate enlargement is my leading thought, not anything worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.06,
      "end_seconds": 281.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "We should do a urine dipstick for urinary symptoms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 282.09,
      "end_seconds": 287.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "We have a slot Tuesday at 9 am, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.8,
      "end_seconds": 296.52,
      "duration_seconds": 8.72,
      "text": "We'll begin with tamsulosin, 400 micrograms, once a day after food, long term. That should help with urinary symptoms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.43,
      "end_seconds": 300.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.21,
      "end_seconds": 319.05,
      "duration_seconds": 17.84,
      "text": "Cut down on caffeine and fluids in the evening. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.94,
      "end_seconds": 324.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Ah, great, thank you for your help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.34,
      "end_seconds": 326.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}